# Ollama Modelfile — locally fine-tuned VidhanAI Llama-3.2-3B (Q4_K_M)
#
# This registers the merged + quantized fine-tuned model (from
# notebooks/export_lora_to_gguf.ipynb) under the Ollama model id `vidhanai`.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Download the Q4_K_M GGUF (~2 GB) from the Kaggle export notebook and
#      rename it to:  vidhanai-lora-q4_k_m.gguf
#   2. Put it somewhere stable, e.g.  D:\models\vidhanai\vidhanai-lora-q4_k_m.gguf
#   3. Edit the FROM line below to that absolute path (forward slashes work
#      on Windows too).
#   4. Register it:
#        ollama create vidhanai -f backend/Modelfile.ollama
#        ollama list          # confirm vidhanai is present
#   5. Run the app with the local fine-tuned model:
#        cd backend
#        set VIDHANAI_USE_OLLAMA=1        (PowerShell: $env:VIDHANAI_USE_OLLAMA="1")
#        python app.py
#      and check bill summaries are stamped  model_version = local_ollama_vidhanai
#
# NOTE: the app sends EXPERT_SYSTEM_PROMPT as the system message per request
# (backend/ai_service.py), so this Modelfile deliberately sets no SYSTEM line —
# the model stays a plain instruct model and the app owns the prompt.
FROM D:/models/vidhanai/vidhanai-lora-q4_k_m.gguf

# Context big enough for a ~6000-char bill excerpt prompt plus a 384-token
# generation. Raise if summaries get cut short.
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
PARAMETER temperature 0.3
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
